  "comment": "The 00 §2 built-in role × permission matrix, derived from the PLANS (not from contracts/permissions.json). Each grant carries the plan citation it is derived from (`NN §S:L` = plans/NN-*.md section S line L; `NN.E.S §S:L` = the feature plan plans/features/*/NN.E.S-*.md; `README T59:118` = plans/features/README.md ruling T59) and a `basis`: `explicit` when the cited text affirms that this role holds this permission (it names the permission code together with the role, or with a phrase the plan uses for exactly that role/role-set - `every member role` for the five member roles, `operator session` for `platform_operator` per 00 §9.1; a row of a role-mapping table counts, its header names the roles), `inferred` when the citation names the permission but not the holder (an endpoint/contract row, or a line naming a different role), so the holder is derived. `permissions` is every catalogue code the plans name (the permission axis of the matrix). The full rule and the inferred table are in README.md. `sensitive` is the plan-derived set of codes that gate secret-adjacent data or return a plaintext secret once (AC5), each with its citation; the matrix test asserts the seeded `permission.sensitive` flags equal it exactly.",
